      {
        "id": 206207,
        "name": "Lord Flash Fire",
        "username": "Lord_Flash_Fire",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lord_flash_fire/{size}/2071_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-10-14T15:08:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I can't believe we've gotten this far without anybody pointing out:</p>\n<div><b>McBehrer wrote:</b><br><blockquote>I'm glad the Fake Walker question was featured. I was pretty proud of that one.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nMcBreher admitted to being Biomancer!\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>i saw that, I just forgot to say anything. Good for you on figuring that out, although now I have to break it to you. The Biomancer clones are just a collective of 8&nbsp; people all coming up with great questions and using the Biomancer facade. When other people try and use it, they find themselves stalked by an unknown presence, that feels… wrong. Eerily similar to themselves, actually. Until they finally end up somewhere ranging from annoying to dangerous, depending on how annoying they were to track down and/or how well they used the Biomancer cover. If they were relatively easy to find out and did a good Biomancer impression, then they might find themselves unconscious for only a few hours Andy wake up in the dumpster behind the &gt;Games building. If they were hard to find and annoying to render unconscious, they may snap out of it on a life raft in the middle of the Atlantic. If sharks come, well, it was your fault. You may have found out McBehrer and me, but there are still 6 of us left! Hahaha! (Jkjk, I’m not Biomancer, but McBehrer has done a good job on this (if he is actually Biomancer.))</p>",
